1. We Take Ownership – Operator/Platform Image Ingestion
The OpenShift Platform team was using a non-approved process to import platform and operator images, creating a security and CAP/Risk gap. Rimas identified the issue and took ownership of the remediation, even though it was outside his original scope. He worked directly with the Platform and Artifactory teams to design an approach aligned to the standard 3PiiP pattern and drove the implementation through migration. The new pipeline has already executed approximately 1,000 times, providing a standardised and secure approach for Operator/Platform image ingestion.
2. We Deliver With Pride – CHRIS
Rimas took technical ownership of CHRIS, a completely new Container Hub reporting and image-scanning service with no existing architecture or implementation to build on. He designed the solution across the backend, data storage and frontend, delivered the initial POC within days and led a two-engineer team to deliver the MVP within one month. He also established consistent engineering tooling and practices across the service. The architecture was designed with future integration into VSaaS, Gating and 3PiiP in mind, ensuring the solution could scale beyond the initial MVP.


We Succeed Together – Cross-Team Technical Leadership
Rimas consistently works across team boundaries to deliver outcomes for Container Security and the wider organisation. He partners closely with SRE, Platform, Artifactory, application teams, ISOs and CSI teams on complex technical decisions and delivery. He also supports team capability through mentoring and has played an active role in interviewing and successfully hiring senior engineers into the wider organisation, including Rory, Mohamed and Vinaya. His ability to assess technical capability, influence across teams and bring the right people into the organisation has strengthened both delivery capacity and the broader engineering capability.
